  "question": {
    "text": "An ideal gas in a cylinder is separated by a piston in such a way that the entropy of one part is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and that of the other part is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. Given that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. If the piston is removed then the total entropy of the system will be:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#215;</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
